#19091
The Heart of the Wood~
   You stand in a hidden glade where the oldest trees of the elven wood
lean together overhead, their leaves glowing gold and green in a light
that has no source.  Fallen leaves lie ankle-deep and smell of every
spring you have ever known.  At the center a single sapling grows from a
ring of white stones, and on the largest stone a verse is cut in elven
script beneath a plain translation in the common tongue.  A path of pale
stones leads east, back toward the crossing.
~
